{"availability":"available","full":"OmarAlkousa/Spectral-Analysis-Web-App","name":"Spectral-Analysis-Web-App","description":"This web app allows you to decompose your signal data or time series using FFT and gives the opportunity to interactively investigate the signal and its spectrum (frequency spectrum, power spectrum, periodogram, and its power spectral density) using the advantage of Plotly package.","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":11,"forks":3,"created":"2023-06-09T13:00:03Z","updated":"2023-07-04T22:11:57Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://omaralkousa-spectral-analysis-web-app-app-yfnwbj.streamlit.app/","topics":["fourier-analysis","periodogram","power-spectral-density","power-spectrum","python","signal-processing","spectral-analysis","streamlit","streamlit-webapp","webapp","welch"],"demo":"https://omaralkousa-spectral-analysis-web-app-app-yfnwbj.streamlit.app/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:08.097Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:08.097Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:08.097Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T03:24:08.097Z","stars":11,"forks":3}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["\"Spectral analysis is based on the Fourier theorem, which states that any waveform can be decomposed into a sum of sine waves at different frequencies with different amplitudes and different phase relationships. When summed, these waves reconstitute the original waveform.\" (Walczak & Chokroverty, 2009)","Spectral analysis can provide valuable insights into the behavior and characteristics of a system or signal. For example, it can be used to identify specific frequencies that are present in a signal, to determine the strength of those frequencies, and to identify any patterns or trends in the data. This information can be used to develop models and algorithms for a wide range of applications, from audio and image compression to medical diagnosis and treatment.","This web app allows you to decompose your signal data or time series using FFT and gives the opportunity to interactively investigate the signal and its spectrum (frequency spectrum, power spectrum, periodogram, and its power spectral density) using the advantage of Plotly package. All you have to do is to upload the file of the signal (.csv) and specify the sampling rate. Additional properties (optional) can be edited like the title of each time and freuquency figures, the labels of the y-axes, and the the color line of each time and frequency data."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OmarAlkousa/Spectral-Analysis-Web-App/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f39b688115bc2d2722f4a5a9b128b554330b01ecac3de0295960876cd53c83a8","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:08.196Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:08.196Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"\"Spectral analysis is based on the Fourier theorem, which states that any waveform can be decomposed into a sum of sine waves at different frequencies with different amplitudes and different phase relationships. When summed, these waves reconstitute the original waveform.\" (Walczak & Chokroverty, 2009)","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OmarAlkousa/Spectral-Analysis-Web-App/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f39b688115bc2d2722f4a5a9b128b554330b01ecac3de0295960876cd53c83a8","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OmarAlkousa/Spectral-Analysis-Web-App/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:08.196Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2023-07-04T22:11:57Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/OmarAlkousa/Spectral-Analysis-Web-App/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T03:24:08.196Z","hash":"f39b688115bc2d2722f4a5a9b128b554330b01ecac3de0295960876cd53c83a8","originalBytes":4669,"storedBytes":4669,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["spectrum","tab.py","calculate","signal","file","frequency","periodogram","power","spectral","psd","used","each",